    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look poised for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by the 69.44 efficiency score of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who benefits from a favorable matchup against the left-handed Triston Rogers. Despite facing a pitcher with a respectable 3.94 xERA, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2019s platoon edge and premium batting order slot make him our most potent asset. Following closely, **Kyle Tucker** (64.80) and **Sam Antonacci** (64.60) offer the high-end production we need; **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s lead-off status against McGreevy, combined with a strong platoon advantage, makes him an essential piece for our stolen base objectives. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (64.30) draws a favorable matchup against Scott, with his 14% platoon boost helping offset the relatively neutral park factors.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Coby Mayo**, who finished with a 38.12 score, narrowly missing the 40-point threshold for active duty. While **Coby Mayo** typically provides power, the matchup against Cease\u2014an elite arm with a 3.02 xERA\u2014proved too daunting for our daily efficiency model, forcing us to prioritize the higher-floor projections of **Miguel Vargas** and **Wade Meckler** despite the latter's modest 54.93 score. We are keeping a close watch on **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 60.92 score is somewhat suppressed by his confrontation with Cease. While **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start due to his irreplaceable talent, his 19% SP skill penalty suggests a grind-it-out game rather than a slugfest. With **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** sidelined on the IL, our depth is thin; we remain optimistic that the high-volume opportunities for **Jackson Merrill** and **Drake Baldwin** will provide enough production to keep us competitive in our 5x5 Roto pursuit.",
